 "summary": "The formal statements say four things about R_k(3), defined as the least n such that every k-colouring of the edges of K_n has a monochromatic triangle: (i) R_k(3)^{1/k} → ∞; (ii) the explicit bound R_k(3) ≥ ((1/(6e^{38}))·k^{1/3}/log k)^k for all k ≥ 2, together with (i); (iii) for every ε > 0 and all large k, (1/4−ε)·k log k ≤ log R_k(3) ≤ (1+ε)·k log k; (iv) log R_k(3) = Θ(k log k). The definitions are faithful. The main caveat is that the lower coefficient in (iii) is 1/4, weaker than the paper's stated exponent 1/3 − o(1).",
 "glossary": [
